"Project does not have access to model “gpt-5.2” – 403 model_not_found error - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/project-does-not-have-access-to-model-gpt-5-2-403-model-not-found-error/1371814)\nciteturn30849search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; Ziyad_G January 16, 2026, 1:45pm 1 ...   * There is currently no option in the OpenAI Dashboard to enable or manage access to this model ... Screenshot 2026-01-16 at 5.49.29 PM985×248 21.5 KB\n\n# Project does not have access to model “gpt-5.2” – 403 model_not_found error\n\nZiyad_G January 16, 2026, 1:45pm 1\n\nI am receiving the following error when trying to use the gpt-5.2 model via the API:\n    \n    `403 – Project does not have access to model \"gpt-5.2\"\n    type: invalid_request_error\n    code: model_not_found\n    `\n\nThe full error message states:\n\n> “Project ‘proj_id’ does not have access to model ‘gpt-5.2’.”\n\ni have verified that:\n\n  * The API key and project are valid\n\n  * Billing is active and in good standing\n\n  * There is currently no option in the OpenAI Dashboard to enable or manage access to this model\n\nWhile GPT-5.2 appears to be available on the ChatGPT website, it does not seem to be accessible via the API for our OPEN AI project.\n\nCould you please clarify:\n\n  1. Is GPT-5.2 officially available for API usage at this time?\n\n  2. If access is restricted, what is the correct process to request enablement for a project or organization?\n\n  3. Is there any expected timeline for general API availability of GPT-5.2?\n\nThank You\n\nScreenshot 2026-01-16 at 5.49.29 PM985×248 21.5 KB--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeprecation notice: upcoming model shutdowns in 2026 - #2 by _j - Deprecations - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/deprecation-notice-upcoming-model-shutdowns-in-2026/1379553/2)\nciteturn30849search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Deprecation notice: upcoming model shutdowns in 2026 ...         \"o3-deep-research-2025-06-26\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-07-23\"}, ...         \"codex-mini-latest\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-01-16\"},  # still working 2026-01-20\n\n# Deprecation notice: upcoming model shutdowns in 2026\n\nAPI Deprecations\n\n_j April 23, 2026, 1:55am 2\n\nThis is an unprecendented massive list of models going away.\n\n  * ISSUE: `gpt-4-turbo` appears in the list, but it is an alias to `gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09` that does NOT appear. Clarification must be made if the destination model will be shut off.\n\n`gpt-4-1106-preview` appears in the listing with a shutoff date of 2026-10-23, but it was already listed and shutoff 2026-03-26, along with gpt-4-0125-preview, and is no longer available on API.\n\nIt seems that the embeddings model has been removed from the listing. If in error, the deprecations page should acknowledge the error blasted by email. Embeddings should be long-life, with a year notice.\n\nAlias pointers should be distinct in their deprecation listing. “This pointer to an actual model is also going away”. Currently it seems we are forced to merely assume the destination model is deprecated.\n\n* * *\n\nHere’s a truth table for programmatic use (without the truth absolutely verified due to ambiguities), with Python inline comments. I included the image and audio models from the newest announcement, previous to that is only chat models.\n    \n    `DEPRECATIONS = {\n        \"gpt-3.5-turbo-0125\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\", \"ft_shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\"},  # official ft-gpt-3.5-turbo shutoff 2026-10-23\n        \"gpt-4-0613\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\", \"ft_shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\"},  # official ft-gpt-4 shutoff 2026-10-23\n        \"gpt-4-1106-preview\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\", \"ft_shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\"},  # ft supported; official ft-gpt-4 shutoff 2026-10-23\n        \"gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09\": {\"shutoff\": \"2026-10-23\", \"alias\